From: MarkJiang-maji <chiang142536@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 00:34:13 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 11/19] monitor v71: resume cumulative cost from Prometheus
 instead of v53

namespace_*_cost* live only in the exporter's memory. On start v71 loaded
them from v53's /metrics, but v53 also keeps them in memory and resets on
every restart (278 restarts on .6), and v53 is being retired.

v71 now asks this cluster's Prometheus for the highest value of its own
series over the last 30 days (LEGACY_BOOTSTRAP_PROMETHEUS_URL); the counters
only grow, so that is the last value before the restart, even after the old
pod's series went stale. An unreachable Prometheus is retried each cycle and
what accrued meanwhile is added on top instead of being overwritten; a
cluster with no history yet starts from 0 without retrying forever.

The default LEGACY_BOOTSTRAP_URL pointed at another site
(120.126.23.25:30044); it is now empty. Checked against .6: the restored
totals equal the live values for all four metrics (178 namespaces).
